From 2b936a81f5e381af492e7fb658c00668364b23e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Evans <noah.evans@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:40:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost: tell the card the host's bus width, and
 let SDHCFG be read

Two defects, both of which stopped a guest driver from reading a single
block through SDHOST.

The bus width is the one that mattered.  "sd: refuse a data transfer whose
two ends disagree about bus width" gave the card the host's width and
refuses a transfer when the two disagree, and hooked it into sdhci only.
bcm2835_sdhost never called sdbus_set_bus_width(), so the card-side width
from ACMD6 was compared against a host that had said nothing, which reads
as one line, and every data transfer on this controller was refused:

    SD: CMD17 in a wrong state: transfer (spec v3.01)
    sd_bus_width_agrees: CMD17 data transfer with the host driving 1 DAT
      line(s) and the card set to 4; ACMD6 and the host's bus width disagree

A guest that had done everything right -- ACMD6, then SDHCFG's WIDE_EXT_BUS
and WIDE_INT_BUS -- got CMD_TIME_OUT on every read.  The width is now set
where SDHCFG is written, the way sdhci sets it where hostctl1 is written,
and on reset where config is cleared, so a four-bit belief in the card does
not outlive a reset and refuse everything after it.

And SDHCFG and SDARG are stored by the write path and were missing from
the read path, so reading either produced "Bad offset" and zero.  Both are
R/W in the BCM2835 documentation.  A driver that prints its own
configuration register to report how it has set the bus up said

    sdhost: card rca 0x3fd3 byte 32768 sectors, ... 4-bit, sdhcfg 0x0

-- a bus it had in fact set up, described from a register that always read
zero.  With both fixed the same driver reports sdhcfg 0x41e and reads the
card.

Checked against the Inferno raspi3b port, whose SD driver uses SDHOST
because the Arasan carries the Pi 3B's Wi-Fi: before, every read failed
and the board found no partition table; after, it reads and writes the
card, mounts FAT32 through it, and makes and mounts a filesystem in the
space above it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost.c b/hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost.c
index f7cef7b..5f7fdc0 100644
--- a/hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost.c
+++ b/hw/sd/bcm2835_sdhost.c
@@ -280,6 +280,19 @@ static uint64_t bcm2835_sdhost_read(void *opaque, hwaddr offset,
     case SDEDM:
         res = s->edm;
         break;
+    /*
+     * SDHCFG and SDARG are stored by the write path below and were not
+     * readable, so a guest that reads either got a "Bad offset" line and
+     * zero.  Both are R/W in the BCM2835 documentation, and a driver that
+     * prints its own configuration register to say how it has set the bus
+     * up reported a bus it had not set up: "4-bit, sdhcfg 0x0".
+     */
+    case SDHCFG:
+        res = s->config;
+        break;
+    case SDARG:
+        res = s->cmdarg;
+        break;
     case SDVDD:
         res = s->vdd;
         break;
@@ -343,6 +356,21 @@ static void bcm2835_sdhost_write(void *opaque, hwaddr offset,
         break;
     case SDHCFG:
         s->config = value;
+        /*
+         * Tell the card how wide the host now thinks the bus is, the way
+         * sdhci does when hostctl1 changes.  Without this the card-side
+         * width from ACMD6 is compared against a host that has never said
+         * anything, which reads as one line, and every data transfer on
+         * this controller is refused:
+         *
+         *   CMD17 data transfer with the host driving 1 DAT line(s) and
+         *   the card set to 4; ACMD6 and the host's bus width disagree
+         *
+         * so a guest driver that does everything right could not read a
+         * block through SDHOST at all.
+         */
+        sdbus_set_bus_width(&s->sdbus,
+                            (s->config & SDHCFG_WIDE_EXT_BUS) ? 4 : 1);
         bcm2835_sdhost_fifo_run(s);
         break;
     case SDVDD:
@@ -418,6 +446,12 @@ static void bcm2835_sdhost_reset(DeviceState *dev)
     s->edm = 0x0000c60f;
     trace_bcm2835_sdhost_edm_change("device reset", s->edm);
     s->config = 0;
+    /*
+     * config has just been cleared, so the host is back to one data line.
+     * Say so, or a four-bit belief left in the card outlives the reset and
+     * refuses everything after it.
+     */
+    sdbus_set_bus_width(&s->sdbus, 1);
     s->hbct = 0;
     s->hblc = 0;
     s->datacnt = 0;
-- 
2.51.0

